;; fault-fetch.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-fetch.s` (P2-SCALAR.3).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py fault-fetch.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "fault-fetch.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-fetch.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05). The third step is the vocabulary's WORD-LESS step (P2-SCALAR.3's extension): the fetch" "at the jump's target faulted, so no instruction word exists — the expectation records the empty" "writes table and the run stops with Stop::FetchFault. Measured on both references: spike reports" "epc = the TARGET with no commit record; sail reports the trap with tval = the target.")
(expectations (program "fault-fetch.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 3) (step (n 0) (insn "lui x1, 0x40000") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000040000000"))) (derivation "0x40000 << 12 = 0x40000000; bit 31 is clear, so the sign extension adds nothing. The address is outside sail-riscv's MainMemory region (0x80000000 + 2 GiB), outside spike's DRAM, and no device on either platform — so all three models fault identically and the guest runs cross-model.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-LUI-AUIPC)")) (step (n 1) (insn "jalr x0, x1, 0") (writes) (derivation "The target is 0x40000000 + 0 with bit 0 cleared = 0x40000000, which IS 4-byte aligned, so no misaligned exception; the transfer happens and the link write goes to x0, which is architecturally discarded — the empty writes table.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.5.1 (D-JALR-LSB); §1.1.1 (x0 hardwired)")) (step (n 2) (insn "the fetch at 0x40000000 — no word fetched") (writes) (derivation "D-FETCH-FAULT-REPORT: an instruction access-fault on the TARGET of a jump is reported ON THE TARGET, not on the jump — the opposite reporting point from misalignment. The fetch at 0x40000000 is outside every declared region, so it raises instruction access-fault, cause 0x01, tval = 0x40000000. No word was fetched, so the step carries none — the vocabulary's word-less step, never a fabricated encoding. Measured: spike epc = 0x40000000 with no commit; sail fetch-access-fault tval = 0x40000000.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.5 (D-FETCH-FAULT-REPORT); RVI-RV64I §3.1.3 + RVI-RV32I §1.1.6 (D-ADDRESS-SPACE: outside every region)")))
